<title>UK: C&amp;W and US West plan joint Russian operation-FT.</title>
<headline>C&amp;W and US West plan joint Russian operation-FT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>British telecommunications group Cable and Wireless and US West, the U.S. regional operator, are planning a merger of their operations in Russia which is designed to challenge the country's incumbent telecoms giants, the Financial Times said on Friday.</p>
<p>The deal would create an integrated Western-owned operator to counter the government-backed companies Rostelekom, and Svyazinvest, the paper said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
